{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe plan-review gate source is commit `952f0825321c755f41edce412ad1fe9f1db9268d`. At that commit, `git show 952f0825321c755f41edce412ad1fe9f1db9268d:src/rebar/_mcp_health.py | wc -l` reports 712 lines. It owns startup handshake, health routing, in-flight instrumentation, and startup checks. The separate `src/rebar/_mcp_serving.py` is 207 lines. It owns `run_mcp`, `run_http_with_grace`, SIGTERM handling, and shutdown. `_mcp_health` re-exports that serving cluster at its file end. `_mcp_serving` imports `install_startup_handshake` from `_mcp_health` and calls it before uvicorn serves.\n\n## End State\n\nA leaf `_mcp_startup_handshake.py` owns only the cohesive initialize-probe call graph: probe-host selection, ASGI request drive, bounded result record, lifespan wrapping, and handshake status. `_mcp_health` remains the health facade. It re-exports existing handshake names. `_mcp_serving` remains the serving facade. It retains HTTP transport, SIGTERM draining, and the existing `install_startup_handshake` call through `_mcp_health`. `mcp_server.py` retains facade-level imports.\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n1. Before coding, recensus the checkout. Record on this ticket the HEAD SHA, the line counts, and the command output above. Treat `952f...` as the reviewed-source attestation.\n2. Move the handshake-only cluster into `_mcp_startup_handshake.py`. The new leaf must not import `_mcp_health` or `_mcp_serving`.\n3. Import plus re-export handshake names through `_mcp_health` before its existing end-of-file serving re-export. Preserve current direct imports and monkeypatch targets.\n4. Keep `_mcp_serving` as the only owner of `run_mcp`, `run_http_with_grace`, `make_sigterm_handler`, and `drain_then_exit`. Preserve its `_mcp_health.install_startup_handshake` import/call shape so the established import cycle remains acyclic.\n5. Do not move health routing, gauge instrumentation, startup store/op-cert checks, HTTP transport, SIGTERM drainage, or shutdown behavior.\n6. Prove the handshake success, non-200, exception, timeout, host selection, lifespan ordering, facade re-export, transport, and shutdown contracts with focused tests.\n\n## File Impact\n\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_startup_handshake.py` — new handshake-only leaf\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py` — health facade imports plus handshake re-exports\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_serving.py` — preserved serving import/call seam plus re-export-cycle contract\n- `src/rebar/mcp_server.py` — only if facade import/annotation verification requires a change\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_health_startup_handshake.py` — handshake result and facade compatibility\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py` — pre-serve handshake, HTTP transport, and graceful-shutdown behavior\n\nCascade flag: true. Re-run semantic, string, dynamic-import, and monkeypatch consumer census at implementation start.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The implementation ticket comment records the current HEAD SHA.\n- [x] The comment records `_mcp_health.py` plus `_mcp_serving.py` line counts.\n- [x] The comment records the gate-pinned `952f0825321c755f41edce412ad1fe9f1db9268d` source attestation.\n- [x] Only the startup-handshake call graph moves into `_mcp_startup_handshake.py`.\n- [x] `_mcp_startup_handshake.py` has no import of `_mcp_health`.\n- [x] `_mcp_startup_handshake.py` has no import of `_mcp_serving`.\n- [x] `_mcp_health` re-exports every existing handshake name.\n- [x] `_mcp_serving` keeps `run_mcp`.\n- [x] `_mcp_serving` keeps `run_http_with_grace`.\n- [x] `_mcp_serving` keeps `make_sigterm_handler`.\n- [x] `_mcp_serving` keeps `drain_then_exit`.\n- [x] `_mcp_serving` retains its `install_startup_handshake` call through `_mcp_health` before uvicorn serves.\n- [x] Existing direct imports plus monkeypatch targets continue resolving through `_mcp_health`.\n- [x] Handshake success preserves its result record.\n- [x] Handshake non-200 preserves its result record.\n- [x] Handshake exception preserves its result record.\n- [x] Handshake timeout preserves its result record.\n- [x] Public-host selection preserves its existing output.\n- [x] Lifespan ordering preserves pre-serve handshake execution.\n- [x] Health routing remains in `_mcp_health`.\n- [x] Gauge instrumentation remains in `_mcp_health`.\n- [x] Startup store/op-cert checks remain in `_mcp_health`.\n- [x] HTTP transport remains in `_mcp_serving`.\n- [x] SIGTERM draining remains in `_mcp_serving`.\n- [x] Focused MCP unit tests pass.\n- [x] Focused MCP facade tests pass.\n- [x] Module-size checks pass.\n- [x] Complexity checks pass.\n- [x] Lint passes.\n- [x] Typecheck passes."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788456901615950001,"uuid":"5019528d-1a0d-4520-a777-fc8eb45d96da"}